{title: Bizarre Love Triangle}
{artist: New Order}
{key: C}
{tempo: 104}
{duration: 2:50}

{start_of_part: (single chord) Intro}
. | [G] . . . |
{end_part}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cmaj7]     Every time I think[D] of you
I get a [Bm]shot right through into a [Cmaj7]bolt of blue
It's no problem of mine, but it's a [D]problem I find
[Bm]Living a life that I can't[Cmaj7]     leave behind
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cmaj7]     There's no sense in [D]telling me
The [Bm]wisdom of a fool won't [Cmaj7]set  you free
But that's the way that it goes, and it's what [D]nobody knows
And [Bm]every day my con[Cmaj7]fusion grows
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cmaj7]Every time I see[D] you falling
I[Bm]  get down on my knees[Cmaj7]     and pray
I'm waiting for that fi[D]nal moment
You[Bm]  say the words that I[Cmaj7]     can't say
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]  [Cmaj7]     I feel fine and I[D] feel good
[Bm]  I feel like I [Cmaj7]never should
Whenever I get this way, I just don't [D]know what to say
Why can't we [Bm]be ourselves like we were [Cmaj7]yesterday?
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Cmaj7]     I'm not sure what this[D] could mean
[Bm]  I don't think you're [Cmaj7]what you seem
I do admit to myself, that if I [D]hurt someone else
Then I'll [Bm]never see just what we're[Cmaj7]     meant to be
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cmaj7]Every time I see[D] you falling
I[Bm]  get down on my knees[Cmaj7]     and pray
I'm waiting for that fi[D]nal moment
You[Bm]  say the words that I[Cmaj7]     can't say
[Cmaj7]Every time I see[D] you falling
I[Bm]  get down on my knees[Cmaj7]     and pray
I'm waiting for that fi[D]nal moment
You[Bm]  say the words that I[Cmaj7]     can't say[G]
{end_of_chorus}